\pard\sb360\sa160\keepn\b\fs31\cf1 Downloader \u8212? product blueprint\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 > **Status: planning and M0 engineering audit in progress. The upstream browser-extension candidate builds, but no Downloader application has been imported, implemented or released here yet.**\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 This is the public collaboration hub for an independently branded, cross-platform **download manager and authorized media-processing platform**. The ambition is to build a credible competitor to established desktop download managers, video downloaders, and browser media tools\u8212?not merely a page that accepts a YouTube URL.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 The product name, software license, commercial model, and final architecture have **not** been approved yet. "Downloader" is a working name. The project owner controls this repository; contributors retain any rights not transferred or licensed under an agreed contribution policy.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 North star\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Create one cohesive experience across:\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 1. **Desktop** \u8212? the flagship application for reliable local downloads, pause/resume, queues, scheduling, file organization, and media conversion.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 2. **Browser extension** \u8212? discover permitted downloads and hand jobs securely to the desktop application.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 3. **Website** \u8212? introduce the product and, in a later milestone, offer a secure browser-based interface for user-owned or explicitly downloadable media.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 4. **Shared engine and optional services** \u8212? reusable jobs, format discovery, media processing, authentication where needed, and diagnostics.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 We benchmark **4K Video Downloader Plus** for video workflows, **Internet Download Manager** for download reliability, **Video DownloadHelper** for browser integration, **JDownloader** for automation, and **Cobalt** for web usability. None has been independently established as the single worldwide "#1" across all categories. See [market analysis](docs/COMPETITOR_BENCHMARK.md).\par
\pard\sa80\par
