\pard\sb360\sa160\keepn\b\fs31\cf1 Instructions for coding agents and AI contributors\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 You are working on **Downloader**, a planned desktop-first download manager, browser companion and authorized media-processing platform. Read this file and the linked product documents before changing code.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Source of truth, in order\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 1. [Legal and security requirements](docs/LEGAL_SECURITY.md).\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 2. [Decisions and unresolved owner choices](docs/DECISIONS.md).\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 3. [Ordered implementation checklist](docs/IMPLEMENTATION_CHECKLIST.md), [product vision](docs/PRODUCT_VISION.md) and [feature matrix](docs/FEATURE_MATRIX.md).\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 4. [Architecture](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) and [roadmap](docs/ROADMAP.md).\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 5. Existing source files, tests and upstream documentation once code is imported.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 If sources disagree, flag the conflict and request a decision. Do not invent requirements or treat proposed architecture as implemented.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Mandatory workflow\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 1. **Inspect before editing.** Check branch, worktree, related docs, existing implementations, dependency licenses and tests. Preserve unrelated changes.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 2. **Classify the request** as investigation, audit, documentation, implementation, testing or deployment.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 3. **Reuse before building.** For each proposed feature, state whether it already exists, needs adaptation, or is genuinely missing. Check license/security compatibility.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 4. **Make a narrow plan** with acceptance criteria and expected tests. Do not attempt the whole roadmap in one task.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 5. **Implement only authorized scope**, using clear interfaces and least-privilege access.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 6. **Verify** with relevant tests/builds and a real, permitted fixture. Separate observed results from assumptions.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 7. **Report** files changed, tests run, remaining blockers and updated feature status.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Cost control for Codex Cloud\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - First task: **audit and gap matrix only**. No bulk code import or large rewrite without owner approval.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Prioritize the smallest end-to-end vertical slice, then expand.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Do not regenerate working code merely to change framework or style.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Cache dependencies in CI, use targeted tests and avoid expensive video downloads in routine runs.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Prefer small deterministic test media and mock adapters; run real-network compatibility tests separately and with permission.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Do not provision cloud servers, enable paid services or deploy publicly without explicit owner approval.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Commit meaningful progress frequently; never rely on disposable task storage for critical work.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Safety and correctness\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Do not circumvent DRM, paywalls, authentication, geo-controls, or copyright restrictions.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Respect YouTube and other platform policies; official APIs do not generally authorize raw media downloading.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Public Chrome extension releases must comply with Chrome Web Store policies (including YouTube restrictions).\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Never log or commit cookies, passwords, tokens, private URLs, user media, secrets or personal identifiers.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Validate remote URLs and redirects; block private network destinations and metadata endpoints; limit resource usage.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Protect local companion APIs against arbitrary websites and cross-origin abuse; use pairing, origin checks and authentication.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Sandbox media parsing/transcoding and use trusted, verified dependencies.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Preserve original copyright and license notices for reused code; use the approved project license only after owner decision.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Project maturity\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 As of the first [M0 audit](docs/M0_AUDIT.md) there is **no application implementation** here. The pinned upstream Chrome extension builds, but no product runtime was imported or tested end to end. A documented upstream feature is **not** an implemented local feature. Do not mark any item Complete until the defined evidence is recorded.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Suggested first deliverables\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 1. Upstream audit including license/SPDX/NOTICE, dependency health and tested builds.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 2. Decision record for base application and shared engine.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 3. Minimal app + extension integration with a user-authorized direct-download test fixture.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 4. Automated tests, packaging and documentation for that slice.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Follow [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) for human review and PR expectations.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 <!-- END AGENTS.md -->\par
