\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Important distinction: source license versus product ownership\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - The owner may control the repository, new original code, brand and deployment **without** acquiring exclusive copyright in upstream code.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **MIT/Apache-2.0** are permissive but still require copyright notices and/or LICENSE/NOTICE preservation; inspect each dependency.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **GPL/AGPL** often require source-availability obligations under distribution or network use; study as references unless the owner explicitly approves the relevant licensing model.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - FFmpeg builds vary in applicable license conditions; generated binaries, external codecs and nonfree flags must be reviewed.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - A separately installed program, embedded library, linked component and copied source code may create **different** obligations. Obtain appropriate legal review before commercial distribution.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Branding and logos are independent of code licenses. Do not reuse third-party trademarks or UI assets as our own.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Audit checklist and evidence format\b0\cf0\par
