\pard\sb360\sa160\keepn\b\fs31\cf1 Proposed architecture (design, not implementation)\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 > **Draft.** The initial implementation has not been chosen or imported. Confirm feasibility with source inspection before making framework-specific commitments.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Core approach\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Desktop first, local by default, one final project repository.** The desktop engine owns download jobs and writes files locally. The browser extension only discovers authorized links and sends authenticated, explicit user-initiated jobs. Media processing is a separate component using FFmpeg for supported files. The website begins as a product presence and expands to a secure optional web service later.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~mermaid\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 flowchart TD\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Extension["Browser companion"] -->|"paired request"| Bridge["Local authenticated API"]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Desktop["Desktop UI"] --> Engine["Download/job engine"]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Bridge --> Engine\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Engine --> Files["Local storage + history"]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Engine --> Media["Media processor"]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Web["Optional web app"] --> Hosted["Isolated hosted API/queue"]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Hosted --> Media\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 The local engine should not depend on the hosted service to download direct files. The hosted API must not accept arbitrary unrestricted URLs.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Preferred first baseline\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Desktop:** Investigate AB Download Manager (Kotlin Multiplatform/Compose) **as-is** before choosing a rewrite.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Extension:** Investigate AB Browser Integration and its native/localhost handoff.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Web UI:** Evaluate ReClip separately. It is **not** already integrated into AB.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Media processor:** Wrap trusted FFmpeg invocation with argument arrays, timeouts, resource limits, job cancellation and sanitized metadata.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Source plugins:** Permissioned adapters for explicitly supported sources; never assume raw media downloads are permitted merely because yt-dlp offers an extractor.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Persistence:** First reuse the chosen desktop application's storage. Add PostgreSQL/Redis only if a later hosted service genuinely needs them.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Avoid premature stack conflict:** Earlier research considered Next.js/FastAPI/Tauri for a greenfield product. The newer AB foundation is Kotlin, and preserving that tested code is the current preferred experiment. A framework rewrite requires evidence that integration is more costly than migration.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Domain boundaries\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Module | Owns | Does not own |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | --- | --- | --- |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Download engine | Transfers, resume/retry, concurrency, state, integrity | Scraping sites, UI rendering |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Browser extension | User intent, permitted URL discovery, secure handoff | Secret storage, FFmpeg execution, arbitrary filesystem paths |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Local bridge | Pairing, auth, rate limits, state/read-only APIs | Open unauthenticated public access |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Media processor | Local file conversions, media probing, safe output handling | Source rights decisions or browser cookie extraction |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Source connector | Rights-reviewed metadata/source resolution | Privilege escalation, DRM circumvention |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Web service (later) | Quotas, auth, bounded jobs, cleanup, abuse protection | Unrestricted server-side URL fetching |\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Job contract (proposed)\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 A job should carry at least:\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Field | Meaning |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | --- | --- |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | id | Stable UUID |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | source_kind | direct_url, local_file, or approved_connector |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | source | Safe reference, not a secret-bearing URL in persistent logs |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | destination | Validated, user-selected destination |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | format_profile | Explicit conversion/quality options or original |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | created_at / updated_at | Time tracking |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | status | Lifecycle state |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | bytes_done / bytes_total | Progress, total may be unknown |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | checksum | Optional integrity expectation |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | retry_count / error_code | Recovery and user messaging |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | provenance | Originating UI, permission decision and source adapter version |\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Proposed lifecycle:\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~mermaid\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 stateDiagram-v2\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   [*] --> Queued\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Queued --> Resolving\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Resolving --> Downloading\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Downloading --> Verifying\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Verifying --> Processing\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Verifying --> Complete\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Processing --> Complete\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Downloading --> Paused\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Paused --> Queued\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Resolving --> Failed\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Downloading --> Failed\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Verifying --> Failed\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Processing --> Failed\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Failed --> Queued: retry\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Queued --> Cancelled\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Downloading --> Cancelled\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Complete --> [*]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Cancelled --> [*]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Workers must be idempotent where feasible; interrupted jobs must persist recoverable state. Successful completion means output is committed safely and integrity requirements passed, not just that a network transfer ended.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Extension-to-desktop security contract\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 1. The user explicitly selects a URL or initiates a permitted capture.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 2. Companion checks allowed origins and authenticates to a paired local helper; no wildcard CORS.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 3. Helper validates URL scheme and destination, enforces limits and creates one job.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 4. Extension receives a job ID and polls/subscribes to permitted progress fields.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 5. Credentials and sensitive request headers remain local and are never echoed to logs or remote websites.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Prefer native messaging or a well-secured loopback bridge after auditing AB's existing protocol; do **not** design a privileged localhost API open to arbitrary tabs.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Future monorepo layout (illustrative)\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 apps/\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   desktop/             # selected existing desktop foundation\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   extension/           # companion browser integration\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   web/                 # optional website\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 components/\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   media-processor/     # local FFmpeg wrapper\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   source-connectors/   # rights-reviewed adapters\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 contracts/             # API schema, versioning, generated clients\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 tests/\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   fixtures/            # small redistributable test files\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   integration/\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 docs/\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 infrastructure/        # only when needed for hosting\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 The folder structure can change after the audit; keep integration **interfaces stable and documented**, not rigidly fixed directory names.\par
\pard\sa80\par
