\pard\sb360\sa160\keepn\b\fs31\cf1 Roadmap with release gates\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 The milestones below are **planned**, not completed. Every milestone ends with a reviewable commit/PR, commands run, test evidence and updated feature status. Do not merge all upstream projects at once.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 M0 \u8212? Audit, choices and legal foundation (first task)\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Outputs:** build/license/dependency/security reports for AB desktop + browser integration and alternative candidates; feature coverage matrix; verified sample test assets; proposed architecture; explicit owner decisions on license and branding.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Exit gate:** One primary base chosen with evidence, license obligations documented, initial OS/browser chosen, risk register reviewed. **No implementation rewrite yet.**\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 M1 \u8212? First working desktop vertical slice (P0)\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Scope:** Build selected desktop foundation; download an authorized HTTPS file, show progress, pause/resume where supported, retry, checksum verification, restart recovery, safe filename handling.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Exit gate:** Reproducible clean install/build; automated local integration tests; no corruption on interrupted transfer; actual output hash matches fixture.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 M2 \u8212? Browser handoff and packaging (P0)\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Scope:** Build selected browser companion; context menu and download capture; pair with desktop; authenticated job handoff; status feedback; browser permissions review.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Exit gate:** Chrome-to-desktop demo succeeds; malicious webpage cannot trigger unauthorized local action; extension package generated; permission inventory documented.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 M3 \u8212? Owned-media processing (P1)\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Scope:** FFmpeg probing, audio extraction, MP4/MKV/WebM, non-DRM HLS/DASH from permitted test sources, subtitles, batch media processing, cancellation and resource limits.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Exit gate:** Deterministic sample fixtures pass; audio/video sync and metadata verified; media failures do not hang UI; shipped FFmpeg binary license recorded.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 M4 \u8212? Website experience (P1)\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Scope:** Product site, download/install guides, optional upload-based converter or rights-reviewed direct URL workflow, clear privacy/terms, accessibility.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Exit gate:** Security review (SSRF, quotas, uploads, retention), responsive usability tests and documented hosting cost; public deployment only by owner approval.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 M5 \u8212? Production-ready release (P1)\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Scope:** CI for supported OS/browser, signed installers and updates, telemetry opt-in, privacy-safe crash reports, localization, release notes, rollback plan, SBOM, security disclosures.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Exit gate:** Clean-machine installation and update tests, accepted security findings, release checklist and support docs.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 M6 \u8212? Competitive expansion (P2)\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Possible scope:** Plugin SDK, CLI/API, scheduled subscriptions for permitted sources, advanced file sorting, remote jobs, mobile companion, AI-assisted indexing of owned media.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Exit gate:** Product usage and support evidence justify each major feature. No automatic commitment to cloud cost.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 How to prevent credit waste\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 For every milestone, maintain this compact progress table in the issue/PR:\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Feature | Upstream status | Local status | Evidence | Next work |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Example: queue | Found in AB docs | Not implemented here | No local test | Audit source/build |\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Rules:\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 1. Complete M0 before choosing a large rewrite.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 2. Work on one milestone and a few acceptance criteria per task.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 3. Run relevant existing tests before adding new code.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 4. Reuse verified packages, keep dependency caches and avoid live-network media tests in every build.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 5. Stop for a decision if a license, platform-policy or material architecture blocker appears.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 6. Do not report or advertise a release until its exit gate is satisfied.\par
\pard\sa80\par
