\pard\sb360\sa160\keepn\b\fs31\cf1 Legal, licensing, privacy and security guardrails\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 This is engineering guidance, **not legal advice**. Get appropriate professional review before releasing a paid product, distributing third-party binaries, or supporting a new platform.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Platform permission boundaries\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 1. **YouTube terms:** Do not assume that being able to view a video grants a right to download it. Terms restrict reproducing/downloading content except where specifically allowed by the service, applicable law, or relevant permissions.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 2. **YouTube API policies:** The YouTube API is not a general audiovisual download API. Its rules restrict downloading, caching and offline use without prior written approval.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 3. **Chrome Web Store:** The store restricts extensions facilitating YouTube downloads; a self-installed development extension is **not** evidence that an extension is eligible for store publication.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 4. **Copyright and authorization:** Support direct downloads/uploads and other sources only where the user has rights and the service permits the operation. Do not provide DRM, paywall, authentication, anti-bot or region-control bypass features.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 5. **Consent and account access:** Never extract user cookies, browser credentials or private tokens without informed consent and an approved design; prefer platform-supported authentication and minimize data handling.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Official sources:\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - https://www.youtube.com/t/terms\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - https://developers.google.com/youtube/terms/developer-policies\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - https://developer.chrome.com/docs/webstore/troubleshooting\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - https://developer.chrome.com/docs/webstore/program-policies/malicious-and-prohibited\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/56100 (official download route for one's own uploads)\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 License governance\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Before using third-party code or shipping binaries:\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Record upstream source, commit, exact license, copyright holders, NOTICE and bundled dependencies.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Generate an SBOM and preserve required license/attribution notices in source and releases.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Inspect FFmpeg build flags/codecs carefully (LGPL versus GPL/nonfree configurations).\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Treat AGPL/GPL and other copyleft code as **reference only** unless the owner approves obligations and code-use design.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Do not copy logos, product names, graphics, protected UI designs or documentation wholesale.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Do not assume GPT/Codex-generated output is uniquely owned or free of third-party license issues.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **The project owner has not chosen a license for original Downloader code.** Public visibility alone is not permission to reuse it commercially.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Threat model: desktop and browser\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Threat | Requirement |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | --- | --- |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Malicious website commands local helper | Pairing token/native messaging, strict origin/extension IDs, no wildcard CORS, user confirmation |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Arbitrary filesystem access | Validate destination, canonicalize paths, limit writable directories |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Unsafe source URL or redirect | Validate each hop, deny local/loopback/link-local/private/reserved endpoints and DNS rebinding |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Untrusted downloaded filenames | Sanitize path separators, control characters, reserved names and collision behavior |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Credential leakage | Secret store/OS keychain; redact logs; short-lived tokens; no cookie dumping |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Malicious media file or playlist | Resource-limited workers, trusted FFmpeg, updates, timeouts and crash isolation |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Unauthorized software updates | Signed builds, verified update metadata, rollback and safe release channels |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Extension over-permission | Manifest V3, minimized host permissions, clear consent, automated permission review |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Data loss | Atomic output rename, checksum, safe temporary-file handling, explicit cleanup |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Supply-chain compromise | Pin/review dependencies, SBOM, vulnerability scanning, provenance and CI protection |\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Threat model: optional hosted services\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Block SSRF to cloud metadata, RFC1918, loopback, link-local, IPv6 internal and localhost hostnames.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Validate redirects and DNS answers on every request; do not proxy privileged credentials.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Restrict protocols, response size, download duration, concurrency, accepted content types and disk quota.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Authenticate users; set per-user and global rate/cost limits; provide job expiry and media deletion.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Never expose storage buckets or private media publicly by default.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Make data retention, privacy policy, abuse handling and takedown contact available before launch.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Prefer local processing to avoid paying for other users' bandwidth and to reduce privacy risks.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Minimum verification before every release\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Rights/permissions and allowed-source checklist.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Dependency and license scan; binary provenance.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Secret scanning and browser permission diff.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Tests for corrupted downloads, redirects, SSRF, malicious paths, retry storms and disk exhaustion.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Clean-machine install/update/uninstall and browser-bridge abuse tests.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Privacy text, security contact and third-party notices updated.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Do not deploy, publish a browser-store listing or claim copyright compliance until these gates are reviewed.\par
\pard\sa80\par
