\pard\sb360\sa160\keepn\b\fs31\cf1 Codex Cloud workflow: build efficiently\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 The owner intends to use GPT-6 Astra/Codex Cloud where available. Model access, task allowances, network access and GitHub permissions depend on the selected environment.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Start in the correct repository\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 1. Connect GitHub to Codex and grant access to **rejoansardar620-lang/Downloader-**.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 2. Create/select a Codex Cloud environment containing this repository.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 3. Configure required development tools, dependency caches and only the network domains genuinely needed.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 4. Give Codex a **single bounded milestone**, not "build every feature".\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 5. Inspect its diff, tests, risks and billable cloud dependencies before approving further work.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 6. Commit/push important work. A new cloud task may not inherit uncommitted changes from an earlier task.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Official overview: https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001545-using-codex-cloud\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 First prompt: audit only\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~text\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 You are the lead engineer for Downloader.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Read README.md, AGENTS.md, docs/START_HERE.md,\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 docs/PRODUCT_VISION.md, docs/FEATURE_MATRIX.md,\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 docs/REFERENCE_REPOSITORIES.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md,\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 docs/ROADMAP.md, docs/LEGAL_SECURITY.md and docs/DECISIONS.md.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 GOAL: Build a reliable commercial-quality desktop-first download\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 manager, browser companion and optional authorized media web UI.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Minimize coding time, compute costs and duplicated functionality.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 THIS TASK IS M0 ONLY. DO NOT BUILD THE ENTIRE PRODUCT.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Audit AB Download Manager and AB Browser Integration first.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Compare ReClip, MediaGrabber, HLS Downloader, Parabolic and the\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 other repositories in docs/REFERENCE_REPOSITORIES.md as needed.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 For each candidate:\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Pin the exact commit and read license/third-party notices.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Check actual source and existing tests, not README alone.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Build in a safe isolated environment if feasible.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Record framework, supported platforms, license obligations,\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   dependencies, maintenance and security risks.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Map requested features to verified upstream / partial / missing.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Keep local repository status distinct from upstream capabilities.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Propose a single smallest Windows + Chrome HTTPS direct-file\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   download vertical slice with measurable acceptance tests.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Update the audit report and docs/DECISIONS.md with proposed choices.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Report every command run and whether it passed or was blocked.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Do not copy upstream code, deploy, buy services or expose secrets.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Stop after M0 and request owner approval for M1.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Follow-up prompt for an approved implementation milestone\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~text\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Implement only milestone [M1/M2/etc] from docs/ROADMAP.md,\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 using the owner-approved ADRs in docs/DECISIONS.md.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 First inspect existing source/tests and list what is reusable.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Preserve licenses/notices and maintain clear module boundaries.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Do not build features already functioning in the chosen base.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Add deterministic tests with authorized fixtures, then run the\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 relevant build and security checks.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Update docs/FEATURE_MATRIX.md with only verified results.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Provide diff summary, test commands/results, unresolved blockers,\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 security and licensing changes, and a short next-step recommendation.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Stop at the milestone boundary.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Anti-waste rules\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Bad pattern | Better instruction |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | --- | --- |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | "Build the whole competitor now" | One milestone with 3\u8211?6 measurable acceptance criteria |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Reimplement queues already in AB | Audit and adapt existing queue APIs |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Import 10 repositories in one commit | Pin and assess, then import minimal reviewed components |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Run full video compatibility on every change | Offline fixture tests; bounded scheduled compatibility tests |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Switch from Kotlin to Tauri without evidence | Build the existing desktop base first, then compare costs |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Claim everything works because it compiles | Validate behavior end-to-end on supported OS/browser |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Rebuild all platforms on every tiny edit | Targeted tests first, full CI at release gates |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Pay for servers before product validation | Local-first architecture, hosting only after approval |\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Reporting format expected from Codex\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 1. **Outcome:** what is now demonstrably usable?\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 2. **Changed files:** bounded list.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 3. **Feature status:** verified complete / partial / blocked / not started.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 4. **Checks:** commands, environment, outcomes and limitations.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 5. **Licenses/security:** new dependencies or risks.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 6. **Next milestone:** one proposed bounded task.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Boundaries\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Do not bypass DRM, paywalls, account protections, YouTube/Chrome policies or unauthorized source restrictions.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Do not harvest browser cookies or repackage third-party source without authorization/license review.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Do not use hidden credentials, create paid resources, or publish releases without the owner's approval.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Do not obscure failures: a network-blocked test is **blocked**, not passed.\par
\pard\sa80\par
