\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Security findings \u8212? must address before release\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **SEC-001 (high-priority design blocker): the upstream loopback API permits unauthenticated requests by default.** In `shared/app/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/abdownloadmanager/shared/storage/appsettings/DefaultAppSettings.kt`, `apiEnabled` defaults to `true` while `apiAuthEnabled` defaults to `false`. The server `integration/server/.../Endpoints.kt` explicitly skips API-key validation on some routes when `apiKeyEnforced` is false; the app binds to loopback `127.0.0.1`. For **our proposed distribution**, make authentication and origin/pairing protections mandatory for downloaded jobs, test malicious webpage requests, and consider disabling HTTP fallback if safe native messaging suffices. Loopback binding alone is not authentication. No exploit is asserted or tested here.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **SEC-002 (review before public Chrome distribution): the upstream MV3 manifest requests broad access.** The built extension contains `host_permissions: ["*://*/*"]`, matches all HTTP(S) pages with its content script, and asks for `cookies`, `webRequest`, `downloads`, `nativeMessaging`, `tabs`, `notifications`, `storage` and `contextMenus`. Establish feature-to-permission justification, reduce scope where feasible, test data minimization and verify store compliance. Do not submit the unreviewed upstream package as our product.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **SEC-003 (user media and URL policy):** Header/cookie forwarding, redirects, private-network requests, DRM, protected sources and platform terms must be reviewed. Only test with content the owner controls or has explicit permission to process. No YouTube extraction demo is a release gate.\par
\pard\sa80\par
