\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 2. Foundation recommendation\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Select exactly two primary upstream projects, conditionally:\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 1. [AB Download Manager](https://github.com/amir1376/ab-download-manager) at **68f0ea6e8ba5cbeb02c92342cd3bf7475378ae68**, for Kotlin desktop engine, queue, persistence, UI and native host.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 2. [AB Browser Integration](https://github.com/amir1376/ab-download-manager-browser-integration) at **bf6811dd8a3ee2b47b94d70e13c2c7e70be7be05**, for MV3 Chrome, Firefox, existing request protocol and browser UX.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Why: a designed integration already exists, the engine has implementation evidence (not merely README claims), and both roots declare Apache-2.0. The alternative Parabolic uses C#/.NET 10 + yt-dlp workflows rather than AB's general direct-file engine; Gopeed uses Go/Flutter under GPL-3.0; Motrix uses Electron/aria2 with extra licensing/runtime concerns. ReClip's current Flask backend accepts arbitrary URLs and is unsuitable as a public service without major SSRF/auth/resource controls.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Evidence for all 17, commit pins and reasons are in [REUSE_DECISION_MATRIX.md](REUSE_DECISION_MATRIX.md). This selection is **not an authorization to copy source code**.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 3. Proposed desktop-first architecture\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~mermaid\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 flowchart TD\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70     B["Chrome user action"] --> E["Extension background"]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70     E --> N["Native messaging host"]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70     N --> C["Desktop integration controller"]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70     U["Desktop UI"] --> C\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70     C --> J["AB job/queue engine"]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70     J --> D["Persisted jobs and download parts"]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70     J --> F["User-approved local files"]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70     F --> V["Integrity checks and safe finalize"]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Existing native messaging manifests already restrict the Chrome extension origin and Firefox extension ID. **Keep that boundary.** The desktop integration handler currently supports both GUI import and a separately authenticated headless API. A browser-originated request must be treated as untrusted input even when native messaging authenticated the extension.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Local HTTP bridge:** The upstream server binds 127.0.0.1 and skips authentication when its optional auth setting is disabled; default is disabled. The extension currently prioritizes HTTP fallback unless native messaging is already connected. For our intended release, require authenticated, version-aware pairing for *every* job-creating route, and prefer native messaging for the first slice. Either remove the unauthenticated HTTP fallback or make it independently secure. See issue #6.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Not in the first slice:** hosted conversion, Redis, PostgreSQL, arbitrary remote job control, AI features, public source extractors and billing. None is needed to prove local file reliability.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb190\sa100\keepn\b\fs23\cf1 Proposed job lifecycle\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~mermaid\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 stateDiagram-v2\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   [*] --> Queued\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Queued --> Resolving\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Resolving --> Downloading\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Downloading --> Paused\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Paused --> Queued\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Downloading --> Verifying\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Verifying --> Complete\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Resolving --> Failed\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Downloading --> Failed\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Verifying --> Failed\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Failed --> Queued: bounded retry\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Queued --> Cancelled\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Downloading --> Cancelled\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Complete --> [*]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70   Cancelled --> [*]\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Compatibility rule:** AB already has download/job/queue model classes and a native messaging request protocol. The first implementation should **adapt its existing shapes**, not create a competing engine or prematurely assert that a newly imagined JSON format is implemented. Before B02, define the smallest version/feature negotiation and compatibility tests around the existing message shapes.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **New bridge validation rules to implement after adoption approval:**\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Only the pinned, user-installed extension ID may invoke native actions; parse a bounded JSON message, reject unknown actions and schema-invalid inputs.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Require user intent, preferably a GUI confirmation for the first authorized direct URL. Reject silently submitted jobs absent an explicit opt-in and authenticated pairing.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Restrict HTTP fallback by strong tokens, origin/Host checking, short timeouts, replay controls and no wildcard CORS; consider disabling it entirely for beta.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Validate allowed URL schemes and redirects, avoid private/loopback fetches when proxying arbitrary remote URLs, and never accept an untrusted absolute destination path.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Sanitize filenames, handle collisions and disk-full/permissions errors, cap concurrency and retries, and never log cookies, Authorization headers or private links.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Persist job state before acknowledging creation; success requires complete/verified output rather than only an HTTP 200 response.\par
\pard\sa80\par
