\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 5. M1 smallest working desktop slice \u8212? after owner approval\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 1. Select a fork/subtree strategy that retains AB upstream provenance and Apache-2.0 notices. Record original commit and any changes.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 2. Reproduce a clean desktop build (Linux first; Windows 11 target) with exact JDK/Gradle/Android-disabled configuration. Keep existing modules and DB implementation.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 3. Use our Python fixture's local HTTPS endpoint with a trusted temporary test cert. The app must download a known SHA-256 file to a user-approved directory.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 4. Test actual progress (bytes/speed), pause/resume (Range+If-Range), retry after truncated response, cancellation, 302 redirect and no-range safe restart.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 5. Test filename/path validation, collision, disk-full behavior, finite retries and failure messages.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 6. Kill/restart app and verify persisted partial state and safe output finalization; compare SHA-256.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 7. Add focused integration tests for each scenario, document clean-build commands and update the checklist only where behavior passed.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **M1 gate:** reproducible Windows 11 binary, authorized HTTPS file download with real progress, verified output checksum, safe cancellation/recovery and no required internet video source.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 6. M2 smallest secure browser slice \u8212? after M1 and owner approval\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 1. Fork the pinned AB extension without reimplementing its existing popup/context-menu code.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 2. Fix TypeScript errors, package MV3 Chrome and document exact compatible extension/desktop versions.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 3. Pair the browser to the native host with registered extension ID, bounded messages and explicit user action.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 4. Send one permitted HTTPS fixture job and observe desktop acknowledgement and progress.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 5. Reject unknown extension IDs, forged origins, unauthenticated localhost HTTP requests and malicious paths.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 6. Review broad host/cookie/webRequest permissions; minimize them without falsely claiming those features work.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 7. Add Chrome install/reload/update smoke test on Windows 11. Do not claim Chrome Web Store eligibility without a policy review.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **M2 gate:** one user action creates exactly one authenticated desktop job; negative tests fail closed; no unauthorized YouTube or protected media features.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 7. Owner approvals required before imports/releases\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 1. **G03:** public product name, identity and trademark/logo policy.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 2. **G04:** original-code license (open-source or proprietary), distribution and contributor terms.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 3. **G05:** first target Windows 11 + Chrome (recommended); secondary OS/browser priorities.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 4. **G06:** scope: authorized direct downloads first, media tools later, optional web service later.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 5. **G08:** CI/cloud usage budget and whether public Actions PR checks may run.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 6. **Gate M0:** approve the exact two upstream commits and Apache-2.0/third-party notice strategy after dependency audit.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 7. **ADR-014:** content source/rights policy and public store/distribution constraints.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Until those decisions are recorded, do not import the full upstream app, claim ownership of third-party code, publish a product, or create paid resources.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 8. Cost-conscious continuation prompt\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 > Continue M0 for Downloader using docs/REUSE_DECISION_MATRIX.md, docs/BUILD_START_PLAN.md and docs/M0_AUDIT.md. Resolve issue #4 only via an environment with permitted verified Gradle 9.8 and JDK 25 binaries; otherwise record the exact blocker. Resolve issue #5 in an approved isolated upstream fork, without hiding TS errors. Harden the protocol described in issue #6 only after owner decisions. Preserve the current original Python fixture, run its 14 tests, and review the manual/PR fixture CI. Do not deploy or import GPL/AGPL code, and do not claim M1/M2 done without a real Windows + Chrome integration test.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Definition of progress:** new code, tests, measured results and durable audit evidence. A passing upstream extension build alone does not make our Downloader application runnable.\par
