\pard\sb360\sa160\keepn\b\fs31\cf1 M0 reuse decision matrix \u8212? 17 source-code candidates\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Reviewed:** 15 November 2026. **Decision status:** engineering recommendation, **NOT owner approval**. Exactly **two primary foundations** are recommended. The other 15 are selective dependencies, deferred connectors, or study references; none is imported into Downloader.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Evidence standard and limitations\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Read the actual repository files using a pinned GitHub default-branch commit, with build manifests, relevant implementation modules, and/or source test directories. This is **source triage**, not a complete 17-project security, licensing, binary, or quality certification.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Checked default-branch commit, repository metadata (license field, archived status, language, commit date), root layout, and selected source/build files for all 17. Full third-party dependency license inventories, SBOMs, automated tests, binaries, and runtime compatibility are **not yet verified** for those projects.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Separately cloned and read source for AB desktop, AB extension, ReClip, and MediaGrabber. **Only the AB extension** was bundled and typechecked in this pass; AB desktop Gradle launch failed. No site-specific extraction tests were run.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - The GitHub license field can be NOASSERTION even when source contains license documents. A root license cannot settle obligations of bundled binaries. Activity indicates maintenance interest, not a passing build.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Use links below as **primary source evidence**, not as code-import authorization. Consult [legal/security requirements](LEGAL_SECURITY.md) and [first audit](M0_AUDIT.md).\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Exactly two selected primary foundations\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb190\sa100\keepn\b\fs23\cf1 1. AB Download Manager \u8212? REUSE/ADAPT, conditional\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Pinned source:** [amir1376/ab-download-manager at 68f0ea6](https://github.com/amir1376/ab-download-manager/commit/68f0ea6e8ba5cbeb02c92342cd3bf7475378ae68), Apache-2.0 root LICENSE, Kotlin/Kotlin Multiplatform + Compose.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Actual code:** downloader/core/src/commonMain/.../DownloadManager.kt persists jobs via IDownloadListDb and supports path/filename validation and collision strategies. queue/QueueManager.kt loads persisted queues. desktop/app/build.gradle.kts wires the engine, monitor, shared app, native messaging launcher and integration server. The downloader/core module uses OkHttp and HLS parser.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Existing integration:** integration/server/.../Endpoints.kt provides /add, /ping, /queues; desktop native messaging host writes Chrome allowed_origins and Firefox allowed_extensions with configured IDs.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Build risk:** wrapper requests Gradle 9.8; gradle.properties specifies jvm.toolchain=25 (the current cloud image provides JDK 21). Wrapper bootstrap cannot reach the binary release asset from this environment. No desktop binary or Windows demonstration exists here.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Security debt:** default loopback HTTP API enabled, API key enforcement disabled; /add supports silent options through the UI integration path. Must harden before public distribution.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Why chosen:** reuse one coherent direct-transfer engine, desktop UI, persistence and native companion instead of rebuilding a general downloader in a new framework.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb190\sa100\keepn\b\fs23\cf1 2. AB Download Manager Browser Integration \u8212? REUSE/ADAPT, conditional\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Pinned source:** [amir1376/ab-download-manager-browser-integration at bf6811d](https://github.com/amir1376/ab-download-manager-browser-integration/commit/bf6811dd8a3ee2b47b94d70e13c2c7e70be7be05), Apache-2.0 root LICENSE, TypeScript/React/Vite.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Actual code:** src/manifest/manifest.chrome.ts emits Manifest V3; src/backend/Backend.ts selects HTTP or native messaging; src/backend/HttpApi.ts calls localhost /add and /ping; src/backend/nativemessaging/NativeMessagingTransport.ts implements message IDs/timeouts; src/linkgrabber/DownloadLinkInterceptor.ts already recognizes HLS .m3u8 requests.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Build evidence:** npm ci PASS; Chrome production build PASS; Firefox production build PASS. Standalone TypeScript check FAILS due an unresolved NativeMessaging import, Manifest author type mismatch, and webext-bridge / type-fest declarations.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Security debt:** all-host content scripts, broad host_permissions and cookies/webRequest/nativeMessaging permissions need minimization and justification. HTTP fallback prioritizes loopback when native is not connected.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Why chosen:** already speaks AB's protocol. Replacing it with MediaGrabber would require a second helper protocol plus extra native executables.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **These two are a compatible candidate pair, not a proved integrated release.** No source-code import until license/brand/platform choices are approved, third-party notices reviewed, and the owner approves the selected commits.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Full decision matrix (all 17)\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Key: REUSE = proposed core foundation; ADAPT = later selective dependency/module after review; REFERENCE ONLY = research architecture/UX, not copying code; DEFER = hold pending scope/policy; REJECT = not suitable as a primary foundation.\par
