\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Feature ownership: reuse, adapt, build or defer\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Initial requirement | Upstream evidence | Work in Downloader | Decision |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | --- | --- | --- | --- |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | HTTP(S) engine, multi-part download and resume | AB downloader/core download manager, HTTP connection/destination and parts | Targeted fixture-driven tests, confirm range fallback and checksum | **REUSE + VERIFY** |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Queue, concurrency, scheduling and restart history | AB queue manager with persisted DB, default settings and downloadable jobs | Measure recovery, schedule behavior, invalid state | **REUSE + VERIFY** |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Download path and naming | AB DownloadManager validates path/filename and collision choice | Threat tests for traversal, platform names, disk full | **ADAPT** |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Browser context menu / handoff | AB extension existing code and desktop native host | Version compatibility, acceptance demo, negative tests | **REUSE + HARDEN** |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Native messaging extension-ID whitelist | AB desktop native messaging manifest source | Brand-specific IDs, user pairing and message validation tests | **ADAPT** |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Local HTTP bridge and silent add | AB optional API-key checks and extension HTTP-first fallback | Require secure default; guard against web-origin abuse and unauthorized silent jobs | **BUILD SECURITY CHANGE** |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Browser permissions | AB extension all-host scripts, cookies/webRequest/nativeMessaging | Narrow hosts and permissions, justify UX and consent | **ADAPT** |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Checksums and integrity declaration | Not yet proven as an end-to-end AB UI acceptance flow | SHA-256 fixture assertion, atomic output verification | **BUILD/VERIFY** |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Controlled HTTPS and disconnect test infrastructure | Our Python local fixture | HTTPS, If-Range, abrupt EOF, CI tests now implemented | **BUILD \u8212? FIXTURE ONLY** |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | HLS detection/stream handling | AB extension .m3u8 and desktop HLS credentials already present | Test permitted fixture before evaluating another HLS codebase | **REUSE + VERIFY** |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | MP4/MP3/containers/subtitles | FFmpeg code and license docs | Safe separate process, bounded jobs, format tests and distribution review | **ADAPT LATER** |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Web interface/backend | ReClip offers a minimal example but accepts arbitrary URLs and in-memory jobs | Original product website later; SSRF/auth/quotas before hosted jobs | **DEFER** |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Site-specific extraction | yt-dlp offers extractors, with permissions/law/policy constraints | Explicit rights/source policy and regression tests | **DEFER** |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Advanced catalog, AI, billing, cross-device sync | No selected core baseline | Demand/cost/security decisions after beta | **DEFER** |\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Distribution / license / security risk register\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Risk | Current evidence | Required before release |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | --- | --- | --- |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | No project license or contributor grant | Downloader lacks a LICENSE; ADR-009 unresolved | Owner chooses ownership/distribution/contribution policy; do not treat this doc as permission |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Apache attribution | Both selected roots have Apache-2.0 LICENSE | Preserve copyright/NOTICE and review nested libraries/assets and license-scanner output |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Kotlin/desktop third-party obligations | Compose, OkHttp, Arrow, HLS parser, JNA, Android tooling, native packager in Gradle scripts | Dependency SBOM, notices, per-binary attribution, platform build conditions |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Browser supply chain | npm lockfile with Vite 4, TypeScript 5.9.3, webext-bridge 6.0.1, type-fest dependency | Fix typecheck, review vulnerable/obsolete packages, SBOM and minimal permissions |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Native/HTTP trust | Native host lists allowed extension IDs; localhost auth disabled by default; silent add possible | Threat model, authenticated pairing and origin rejection tests |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | FFmpeg | LICENSE.md LGPL baseline and GPL components when enabled; vendor builds differ | Approve exact binary/configuration and notices, avoid unreviewed codecs |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | MediaGrabber native binaries | THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md identifies a GPLv3 FFmpeg Windows bundle | Avoid accidental incompatible distribution from selective code import |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | GPL/AGPL alternatives | Gopeed, aria2, Cobalt, MeTube, Pinchflat, Tube Archivist, archived UI | Reference only unless explicit owner/legal approval and obligations fulfilled |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Web URL handling | ReClip accepts arbitrary URL passed to yt-dlp; in-memory jobs; no visible quotas/auth | Do not deploy as a public fetch service; explicit SSRF/redirect/limit design |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Platform policies | Chrome Web Store specifically flags extensions facilitating YouTube downloads | Test with authorized direct files, complete store policy review before distribution |\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Confidence and next evidence needed\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **High confidence in integration direction:** two primary roots are Apache-2.0 and communicate through a designed native/HTTP bridge; extension bundling is reproducible.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Moderate confidence in feature reuse:** source code for engine/DB/queue/HLS is present, but no end-to-end desktop tests or Windows verification performed in this audit.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **Low confidence in release readiness:** Java 25 toolchain and Gradle bootstrap, TypeScript typecheck, transitive license/SBOM, browser permissions, localhost API authentication and store policy gates remain open.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - **No verified performance ranking:** none of 17 was speed-benchmarked against the same authorized server/hardware.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Final M0 recommendation to owner:** adopt **AB Download Manager + AB Browser Integration** only after approving license, scope, branding and Windows/Chrome target. Keep one Kotlin engine, its natural companion extension, and add only evidence-backed adapters. Do not import ReClip, MediaGrabber, Gopeed, Motrix or any GPL/AGPL project as a second core.\par
\pard\sa80\par
