\pard\sb360\sa160\keepn\b\fs31\cf1 Contributing to Downloader\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Thanks for helping create a reliable, privacy-conscious download manager. The project is currently **documentation-first**: architecture and candidate repositories exist, but application code has not yet been imported or validated.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Before your first contribution\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 1. Read [the quick start](docs/START_HERE.md), [vision](docs/PRODUCT_VISION.md), [feature matrix](docs/FEATURE_MATRIX.md) and [legal/security requirements](docs/LEGAL_SECURITY.md).\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 2. Check [open decisions](docs/DECISIONS.md) and the [roadmap](docs/ROADMAP.md).\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 3. Open or select an issue describing a narrow outcome. Avoid duplicate work and giant PRs.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 4. For proposed upstream code, provide the exact repository, commit/tag, license, dependency tree and preservation requirements.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 5. Discuss nontrivial changes to architecture, licenses, distribution or network behavior before implementation.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Current contribution opportunities\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Verify reference-repository licenses, recent activity and dependency security.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Build a feature coverage matrix from **actual source inspection and test results**.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Identify usable direct-download fixtures with explicit redistribution/test permission.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Design the protocol for extension-to-desktop job handoff.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Improve security and acceptance criteria.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Propose the initial CI matrix (Linux analysis/build, Windows packaging, browser smoke tests).\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 After the owner decides the software license and contribution policy, implementation issues can be opened for the first vertical slice.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Pull request checklist\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - [ ] Linked issue and succinct problem statement.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - [ ] Single focused change; unrelated user changes preserved.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - [ ] Clear distinction between implemented, tested and proposed behavior.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - [ ] Tests/documentation updated, commands and results reported.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - [ ] New dependencies justified with license, security and maintenance notes.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - [ ] No secrets, session data, unapproved binaries, media archives or generated downloads.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - [ ] No DRM, paywall, access-control or rights circumvention.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - [ ] License and provenance information supplied for any imported upstream code.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Engineering conventions (provisional)\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Keep browser, desktop, web and engine modules independent with versioned API contracts.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Prefer typed interfaces, explicit errors, dependency injection and deterministic tests.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Handle cancellation, retry, resume and crash recovery as first-class state transitions.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Include an end-user recovery message with each operational failure.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Do not add a dependency solely to avoid writing a few lines of simple code; conversely, do not rewrite mature infrastructure.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - Use existing formatting and testing scripts once a chosen base repository is imported.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Licensing and ownership\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Project license and contribution terms are not yet selected.** Do not assume public visibility means permissive licensing. Contributors retain rights unless an applicable license/contribution agreement says otherwise. Open issues and documentation suggestions are welcome; contact the maintainer before submitting substantial application code or copying third-party components.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Vulnerability reporting\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Do not publish exploit details, credentials or sensitive reproduction data in public issues. Use GitHub's private vulnerability reporting/security advisory mechanism if enabled, or contact the repository owner privately first.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Proposed PR template\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 See [.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md](.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md). Be factual: never mark a feature ready because it works only in an upstream repository.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 <!-- END CONTRIBUTING.md -->\par
