\pard\sb360\sa160\keepn\b\fs31\cf1 Security policy\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 This repository is currently a **planning/documentation project**, with no published application build. Security-sensitive issues may still arise in future implementation work or dependencies.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Reporting a vulnerability\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Do **not** publish proof-of-concept exploits, private tokens, user files or personal information in a public issue.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Prefer GitHub private vulnerability reporting or a GitHub Security Advisory if the owner enables it. Otherwise, contact the repository owner privately through their GitHub profile and request a secure reporting channel. The project has no designated security email or response-time SLA yet.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Engineering policy\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 All contributors should read [legal and security guardrails](docs/LEGAL_SECURITY.md). In particular, local desktop bridges, native messaging, untrusted URLs, redirect handling, FFmpeg inputs, browser permissions and supply-chain dependencies require careful review.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Only report tested security behavior; no features have been security-audited in this repository at its documentation bootstrap.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 <!-- END SECURITY.md -->\par
\pard\sa80\par
