\pard\sb360\sa160\keepn\b\fs31\cf1 Deterministic direct-download fixture (M0/M1)\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 The server is **our original implementation**, independent of candidate upstream applications. It provides a small HTTP test target for the Downloader desktop engine and browser handoff. It never fetches outside URLs, accesses local files, or processes real user videos.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Start\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 From repository root, with Python 3.10+:\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~sh\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 python3 -m tools.fixtures.http_fixture --port 8765\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 The server binds **only to 127.0.0.1**. A port of `0` assigns an available loopback port. Run tests:\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~sh\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 The test suite generates a temporary self-signed certificate with the local\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 OpenSSL CLI and tests real HTTPS with certificate verification **enabled**.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 The temporary certificate and key are removed when tests finish.\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 For a manual HTTPS run, supply your own local test certificate and key:\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~sh\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 python3 -m tools.fixtures.http_fixture --port 8765 \\\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70     --tls-cert /path/to/test-cert.pem --tls-key /path/to/test-key.pem\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 ~~~\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 The HTTPS client must trust that specific test certificate. Never disable\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 TLS verification globally to make a test pass.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | URL | Behavior | Expected |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | --- | --- | --- |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | `/file.bin` | Fixed 16 KiB binary payload | HTTP 200, `Accept-Ranges: bytes`, deterministic SHA-256 |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | `/file.bin` with `Range: bytes=0-8191` | First half | HTTP 206 + correct `Content-Range` |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | `/file.bin` with `Range: bytes=8192-` | Second half | HTTP 206; concatenate pieces to obtain exact payload hash |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | `/file.bin` with `Range: bytes=99999-` | Invalid offset | HTTP 416 + `Content-Range: bytes */16384` |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | `/no-range.bin` | Deliberately ignores Range | HTTP 200, full body; a downloader must restart safely |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | `/health` | Readiness | HTTP 200 `ok` |\par
\pard\f1\fs15\sa0 | Any unknown URL | No external proxy | HTTP 404 |\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 Additional controlled test endpoints and behaviors:\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - /file.bin with a matching If-Range ETag: 206 partial resume.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - /file.bin with a stale If-Range ETag: 200 full response (restart).\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - /drop.bin: connection closes after 2048 bytes of a declared 16 KiB response; the client must report a truncated transfer.\par
\pard\li200\fi-100\fs19\sa35 - /redirect.bin: 302 with a local Location header pointing to /file.bin.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 When M1 imports the approved engine, use these endpoints for direct, interrupted/resumed, invalid-range, redirect, TLS and integrity tests. The fixture supports only single byte ranges and local redirects. It does not model authenticated remote sources, bandwidth throttling, HLS/DASH, multirange replies or full crash/restart behavior.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 CI is defined in .github/workflows/fixture-tests.yml. It runs for relevant pull requests or on manual invocation, with no GPU or hosted downloader deployment. Passing these tests does not prove the future desktop app works.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 <!-- END tools/fixtures/README.md -->\par
\pard\sa80\par
