\pard\sb190\sa100\keepn\b\fs23\cf1 1. Initial request: downloader website or extension\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **User:** \u8220?I would like to create youtube video downloader extension/website can u pls guide\u8221?\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Discussion/outcome:** Initial exploration of Next.js/TypeScript frontend, FastAPI or equivalent backend, optional FFmpeg, browser Manifest V3 and a shared architecture. Features discussed included URL input, quality selection, audio/video conversion, queues, progress, playlists and batching. These were prospective features\u8212?not implemented ones. YouTube terms and Chrome Web Store restrictions were flagged; production scope must be authorized media.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb190\sa100\keepn\b\fs23\cf1 2. Existing public repositories\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **User:** \u8220?I want to find any public repo available that type of\u8221?\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Discussion/outcome:** Examined website/extension examples: MeTube, ReClip, Pinchflat, YouTubeDL-Material, Tube Archivist, yt-dlp-web-ui; Super Video Downloader, MediaGrabber, HLS Downloader, Tube Archivist Companion, Media Grabber. Repositories were presented as study references and possible starting points, not an approved code merger. The final consolidated study list was narrowed/expanded into 17 project references; see docs/STUDY_REPOSITORIES.txt.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb190\sa100\keepn\b\fs23\cf1 3. Software belonging to the project owner, and Codex Cloud\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **User:** \u8220?i want to create my own software system which is belong to me which repo should i consider and then gpt astra codex will code and build for my own and can astra in codex cloud build\u8221?\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Discussion/outcome:** Initial recommendation emphasized ReClip and MediaGrabber because their reported MIT licenses are comparatively permissive. Explained that owning the new project's branding, infrastructure and original code does **not** transfer copyright ownership of upstream components. Discussed Codex Cloud as a coding/testing aid, not a guarantee of production readiness, platform approval, or deployment. No release or ownership/legal approval was made.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb190\sa100\keepn\b\fs23\cf1 4. Single repo versus combination\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **User:** \u8220?is combination repo or single repo should i take if i want to build every feature\u8221?\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Discussion/outcome:** Recommended reviewing multiple upstreams, integrating only compatible components, and publishing a **single well-structured product monorepo**. Initial options mentioned ReClip (web), MediaGrabber (extension), HLS Downloader (non-DRM media), FFmpeg, yt-dlp (rights-reviewed), and MeTube as an AGPL reference. Important correction later: this was an exploratory combination; do not blindly merge.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb190\sa100\keepn\b\fs23\cf1 5. Ambition: a top competitor\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **User:** Wanted to create software competitive with the best available download managers\u8212?not a simple single-site link downloader.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Discussion/outcome:** Benchmarked 4K Video Downloader Plus (media workflows), Internet Download Manager (recovery/acceleration), Video DownloadHelper (browser media detection), Cobalt (web UX), and JDownloader 2 (queues/automation). These are **feature benchmarks**, not evidence of an objective market #1 ranking. Product differentiated by reliability, privacy, local-first operation, strong UX, organization, security and quality engineering. Early speculative Tauri/Next.js/FastAPI architecture was later superseded by the recommendation to retain mature Kotlin/Compose upstream desktop internals.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\sb190\sa100\keepn\b\fs23\cf1 6. Avoid unnecessary Codex spending\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **User:** \u8220?or anything would u like to say which is publicall available in market but codex is building and wasteing my credit so we can include them right now. to achive our main goal\u8221?\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Discussion/outcome:** Identified [AB Download Manager](https://github.com/amir1376/ab-download-manager) and its [browser companion](https://github.com/amir1376/ab-download-manager-browser-integration) as stronger starting candidates for a desktop-first system. Added Gopeed, Motrix and aria2 to research comparisons. Recommended feature coverage analysis before coding: REUSE / ADAPT / BUILD with licenses, tests and verification. Core rule: do not ask Codex to rebuild mature functionality without demonstrating an actual gap. AB desktop and browser extension eventually became **exactly two provisional primary foundations**.\par
\pard\sa80\par
