\pard\sb260\sa120\keepn\b\fs26\cf1 Technical findings to preserve\b0\cf0\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **AB desktop:** Downstream source investigation described Kotlin/Compose architecture, persistent job/queue models, HTTP download handling, local integration, and native messaging host. Never infer all of these are proven working in our product\u8212?they belong to the upstream candidate. Gradle wrapper 9.8 and JDK 25 requirements deserve controlled build verification.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **AB extension:** Pinned source's Chrome and Firefox bundles were built successfully. Standalone TypeScript validation failed with missing native-messaging import and manifest/dependency typings. Chrome packaging in upstream is not the same as a working handoff in our product.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Integration security:** Some upstream localhost HTTP paths can run with authentication disabled by default. Treat localhost as untrusted from webpage contexts; secure auth, origin/extension identity, CSRF, SSRF, redirects, paths, cookies, token storage and testing are required. Native messaging is preferred where supported.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Dependency review:** Previous test reported two high-severity findings in an upstream extension dependency tree. Re-run in the approved fork and determine exploitability and remediation before release.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\f0\fs19\sa70 **Original fixture:** `tools/fixtures/http_fixture.py` provides deterministic local HTTP behavior, with Range/no-Range/interrupt/redirect/HTTPS cases; `tests/test_http_fixture.py` reached 14/14 passes in the earlier run. Verify current CI rather than trusting this snapshot alone.\par
